This is the distribution of the Python package abc-sysbio

#################################
# DEPENDENT PACKAGES
#################################

Before trying to install and use abc-sysbio you MUST first install the following packages

	numpy
	matplotlib
	Scientific	

If you wish to use the SBML interface in abc-sysbio you must also install

	libSBML

If you wish to use abc-sysbio for inference in ODE models you must also install
	
	scipy

If you wish to use abc-sysbio on Nvidia GPUs you must also install
	
	pycuda

For instructions and help on how to install these packages see DEPENDENCIES in the doc/ folder


#################################
# LINUX/MAC INSTALLATION 
#################################

Once the required dependent packages have been installed, abc-sysbio is installed via the standard distutils interface. The command

python setup.py install 

will place the module abcsysbio into the standard folder, usually something /usr/lib/python2.6/site-packages/ on Linux, depending on the version of python you are using.
It also places two executable Python scripts called run-abc-sysbio and abc-sysbio-sbml-sum into the standard location, usually /usr/bin on Linux.
if you wish to install to a custom location you can use the command

python setup.py install --prefix=/path/to/custom/location/

The current directory should also be placed into the python path. For bash type shells (default on MAC) do 

export PYTHONPATH=$PYTHONPATH:.

for C type shells do

setenv PYTHONPATH $PYTHONPATH:.

Note that this can be added to your .bashrc or .cshrc.

If everything is installed correctly it should then suffice to do

run-abc-sysbio -h

to get a list of options printed. 

In addition the abcsysbio module can be used like any other Python library.



#################################
# CONTENTS OF PACKAGE		 
#################################

abcsysbio/ is the python module containing all the source code for the approximate Bayesian computation algorithms
doc/ contains the package documentation Manual.pdf and DEPENDENCIES which contains instructions on how to install dependent packages.
examples/ contains the SBML models and input files reproduce Examples 1, 2, 3 and 4 in the package documentation.
scripts/ contains two scripts run-abc-sysbio and abc-sysbio-sbml-sum, that enable easy use of the package for the most common applications.
data/ contains MersenneTwister.dat which is an initialization file for the parallel MersenneTwister obtained from http://www.jcornwall.me.uk

For more details, refer to the package documentation.

##############
